  "notes": "Clean lane: no claim met the quantified-exploit bar (ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-002/003). Considered and dropped: (1) bootstrap.go:71-72 opens os.TempDir()/smine-bootstrap.log 0o644 with symlink-following O_CREATE|O_APPEND; on macOS and Windows TempDir is a per-user 0700 directory, so another local user cannot pre-plant or read it there. Exposure exists only on a shared Linux /tmp, which this chunk does not show to be a supported platform. The known finding correctness-BLK-5-r1 already moves this log, which removes the surface. (2) sameOriginGuard (server.go:398-438, unchanged by this diff) trusts Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin and never checks Host against loopback, so a DNS-rebinding page can still reach mutating routes. The diff adds new sinks of that class: POST /welcome/bootstrap with free-text extra-prompt into a 6h headless run on the routine token, POST /profile/style writing the globally injected style-profile.md, and POST /profile/test running a paid call. The guard itself is pre-existing, and the bind address and port live in cmd/, so the exploit cannot be quantified here. Cross-chunk items for the station: (a) cmd/bootstrap/run.sh's handling of BOOTSTRAP_EXTRA_PROMPT. bootstrapEnv (bootstrap.go:182-188) rejects only quotes and newlines, not $, backticks or backslashes, so an eval or unquoted interpolation in run.sh would allow shell injection. (b) whether run.sh echoes the token into the bootstrap log (ACTION-REVIEW-LOG-004). (c) whether sessions.ArchiveScope/UnarchiveScope/DeleteScope (internal/sessions) reject path-traversal names that arrive via r.PathValue at sessions.go:179/188/197. (d) the server's listen address, which the DNS-rebinding exposure in (2) depends on. Scope: no file removed (ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004).",
